.TH MIRROR-DEDUPE 1 "June 2026" "mirror-dedupe 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mirror-dedupe \- Ubuntu/Debian mirror synchronisation with global deduplication via hardlinks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mirror-dedupe
.RB [ \-\-help ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.RB [ \-\-config-dir
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-sync ]
.RB [ \-\-mirror
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-dedupe-only ]
.RB [ \-\-sweep-pool ]
.RB [ \-\-scan ]
.RB [ \-\-out
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-name
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-dest
.IR DEST ]
.RB [ \-\-upstream
.IR URL ]
.RB [ \-\-releases
.IR DISTS ]
.RB [ \-\-architectures
.IR ARCHES ]
.RB [ \-\-components
.IR COMPS ]
.RB [ \-\-gpg-key-url
.IR URL ]
.RB [ \-\-collapse-dists ]
.RB [ \-\-list ]
.RB [ \-\-activate
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-deactivate
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-test
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-reinitialise
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-list-repos ]
.RB [ \-\-relink-pool ]
.RB [ \-\-snapshot
.RI [ NAME ]]
.RB [ \-\-list-snapshots
.RI [ NAME ]]
.RB [ \-\-restore-snapshot
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-delete-snapshot
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-stats
.RI [ NAME ]]
.RB [ \-\-stats-reset
.RI [ NAME ]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mirror-dedupe
synchronises Debian/Ubuntu package repositories into a pool-based,
content-addressable store and uses hardlinks for global deduplication
across all mirrored repositories.  Both the repository tree and the
deduplication pool are always subdirectories of \fBmirror_root\fR, which
guarantees they reside on the same logical volume \(em a requirement for
hardlink-based deduplication.
.PP
Modes of operation:
.IP \(bu 3
\fB\-\-sync\fR: build the sync tree, fetch Release/Packages
metadata, partition package stanzas by hash prefix, download missing
pool entries, hardlink into repo trees, and clean up.
.IP \(bu 3
\fB\-\-scan\fR: probe an upstream repository, discover
distributions/components/architectures, and generate a YAML config file.
.IP \(bu 3
\fB\-\-sweep-pool\fR: walk the pool and remove orphaned files (those whose
link count has dropped to 1).
.IP \(bu 3
\fB\-\-dedupe-only\fR: run only the deduplication phase against an
already-synced repo tree.
.IP \(bu 3
Management operations: \-\-list, \-\-activate, \-\-deactivate, \-\-test,
\-\-reinitialise, \-\-snapshot, \-\-restore-snapshot, \-\-delete-snapshot,
\-\-stats, \-\-list-repos, \-\-relink-pool.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-v
Show program version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-config-dir " " \fIDIR\fR
Path to the configuration directory (default: /etc/mirror-dedupe).
The directory must contain \fBmirror-dedupe.conf\fR and may contain
\fBrepos-available/\fR and \fBrepos-enabled/\fR subdirectories.
.TP
.BR \-\-sync
Run the full sync pipeline for all enabled mirrors (or a single mirror
when \-\-mirror is given).
.TP
.BR \-\-mirror " " \fINAME\fR
Sync only the named mirror (used with \-\-sync).
.TP
.BR \-\-dedupe-only
Skip metadata sync and only hardlink pool entries into the repo tree.
.TP
.BR \-\-sweep-pool
Remove orphaned pool entries (files whose st_nlink equals 1).
.TP
.BR \-\-scan
Discover upstream metadata and generate a repo config file.  Requires
\-\-name and \-\-out.  Additional scan options are listed below and
documented in mirror-dedupe-scan(1).
.TP
.BR \-\-name " " \fINAME\fR
Repository name (required for \-\-scan).
.TP
.BR \-\-dest " " \fIDEST\fR
Destination path relative to mirror_root/repos (defaults to \-\-name).
.TP
.BR \-U ", " \-\-upstream " " \fIURL\fR
Upstream URL(s) for scanning.  May be specified multiple times.
The first URL is the primary; subsequent entries are fallbacks.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-dist ", " \-\-release " " \fIDIST\fR
Override distribution/suite.  May be specified multiple times.
When any \-\-dist/\-\-release/\-\-releases flag is given, the scanner uses
exactly those suites.  The special value "all" writes every discovered
suite into the config and disables automatic distribution expansion.
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-releases " " \fIDISTS\fR
Comma-separated list of distributions/suites.
.TP
.BR \-\-arch " " \fIARCH\fR
Architecture to include.  May be specified multiple times.
.TP
.BR \-\-architectures " " \fIARCHES\fR
Comma-separated list of architectures.
.TP
.BR \-\-component " " \fICOMPONENT\fR
Component to include.  May be specified multiple times.
.TP
.BR \-\-components " " \fICOMPONENTS\fR
Comma-separated list of components.
.TP
.BR \-\-repo-type " " \fITYPE\fR
Force a specific repo type (e.g. "apt") for unusual layouts.
.TP
.BR \-G ", " \-\-gpg-key-url " " \fIURL\fR
Explicit GPG key URL for this repository.  The scanner checks that the
URL is reachable before writing the config.
.TP
.BR \-\-collapse-dists
Collapse discovered distributions to base suites where possible.
.TP
.BR \-\-no-collapse-dists
Do not collapse discovered distributions; emit all variants explicitly.
.TP
.BR \-\-out " " \fIDIR\fR
Output directory for \-\-scan results (required for \-\-scan).
.TP
.BR \-\-list
List available mirrors, showing which are active (repos-enabled) and
which are inactive (repos-available only).
.TP
.BR \-\-activate " " \fINAME\fR
Activate a mirror by creating a symlink in repos-enabled/.
.TP
.BR \-\-deactivate " " \fINAME\fR
Deactivate a mirror by removing its symlink from repos-enabled/.
.TP
.BR \-\-test " " \fINAME\fR
Test a mirror configuration: check upstream reachability, GPG key URL,
and print a summary of what will be synced.
.TP
.BR \-\-reinitialise " " \fINAME\fR
Snapshot a repo, then remove its data directory.  Activation status is
preserved.  Requires interactive PIN confirmation (or \-\-force).
.TP
.BR \-\-list-repos
List all known repos (config-based and additional).
.TP
.BR \-\-relink-pool
Re-link pool hashes with all managed repos and snapshots.  Useful after
manual pool manipulation.
.TP
.BR \-\-snapshot " " \fI[NAME]\fR
Create a hardlink snapshot of a repo dest directory or ALL repos.
Snapshots are stored under mirror_root/repos/Snapshots/.
.TP
.BR \-\-list-snapshots " " \fI[NAME]\fR
List available snapshots for a repo or ALL.
.TP
.BR \-\-restore-snapshot " " \fINAME\fR
Restore a snapshot.  Accepts NAME[:TS] format; defaults to the latest
snapshot for NAME.
.TP
.BR \-\-delete-snapshot " " \fINAME\fR
Delete a snapshot directory.  Requires interactive PIN confirmation
(or \-\-force).
.TP
.BR \-\-stats " " \fI[NAME]\fR
Print sync statistics for a repo dest or ALL.
.TP
.BR \-\-stats-reset " " \fI[NAME]\fR
Truncate stats.ndjson for a repo dest or ALL.  Requires interactive PIN
confirmation (or \-\-force).
.TP
.BR \-\-force
Bypass PIN confirmation on destructive operations.
.TP
.BR \-\-no-backup
Skip current-state backup before a restore operation.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.SS Global configuration (\fImirror-dedupe.conf\fR)
.TP
.I mirror_root
Root directory for all mirror data.  The repository tree is stored under
\fB<mirror_root>/repos\fR and the content-addressable pool under
\fB<mirror_root>/pool\fR.  Both subdirectories always reside on the same
logical volume.  Default: \fB/srv/mirror\fR.
.TP
.I architectures
Global architecture mask.  Only architectures present in both this list
and each mirror's own list are synced.  "*" or "all" means passthrough.
Default: "*".
.TP
.I collapse_distributions
When true, collapse distribution directory names (e.g. "dists/stable"
to "stable").  Default: false.
.TP
.I parallel_downloads
Number of concurrent downloads per-repo.  Default: 10.
.TP
.I max_concurrent_syncs
Maximum number of repos to sync simultaneously.  Default: 2.
.TP
.I connect_timeout
Connection timeout for curl in seconds.  No \-\-max-time is sent;
downloads run as long as upstream delivers bytes.  Default: 10.
.TP
.I max_retries
Maximum retries for failed downloads.  Default: 2.
.TP
.I sweep_pool_after_sync
Whether to run a pool orphan sweep automatically after the last repo
finishes syncing.  Default: false.
.TP
.I log_colour
Terminal colour scheme.  Valid values: DEFAULT, DARK, LIGHT, NONE.
Default: DEFAULT.
.TP
.I log_colour_bg
Background colour for log output.  Valid values: NONE, DARK, LIGHT.
Default: NONE.
.TP
.I additional_repos
List of repos not in repos-enabled/ but recognised by \-\-list-repos,
\-\-delete, snapshot ops, and Config.resolve_dest().  Each entry has a
name and dest (relative to mirror_root/repos or absolute).
.SS Per-mirror configuration (\fIrepos-available/*.conf\fR)
Each YAML file defines one repository mirror:
.TP
.I name
Mirror identifier (required).
.TP
.I dest
Local destination path relative to mirror_root/repos.
.TP
.I repo_type
Repo type override (e.g. "apt").  Normally auto-detected.
.TP
.I upstreams
List of upstream repository URLs.  The first healthy upstream is used
for each file; fallbacks are tried on failure.
.TP
.I architectures
List of architectures to mirror (e.g. amd64, arm64).
If absent, all architectures from the Release file are used.
.TP
.I components
List of repository components (e.g. main, universe, multiverse).
If absent, all components from the Release file are used.
.TP
.I distributions
List of releases/suites to mirror (e.g. noble, jammy).
.TP
.I expand_distributions
Controls automatic pocket expansion at sync time.  When true (the
default if the field is absent), a base distribution like "noble" is
automatically expanded to include "noble-updates", "noble-security",
"noble-backports", and "noble-proposed" \*(em so a single entry in
\fBdistributions:\fR results in 5 suites being synced.  Expansion only
applies to distributions that do not already contain a hyphen (e.g.
"noble-pgdg" is left as-is).  Set to false to sync only the
distributions listed, with no automatic expansion.
.TP
.I gpg_key_url
URL to the repository's GPG signing key.
.TP
.I gpg_key_path
Relative path under mirror_root/repos where the GPG key is stored.
.TP
.I params
Optional per-repo parameter overrides:
.RS
.TP
.I discovery_method
Upstream layout discovery method: "html_bfs" or "explicit".
.TP
.I log_colour / log_colour_bg
Per-repo log colour overrides.
.TP
.I parallel_downloads
Per-repo concurrency override.
.RE
.SH DEDUPLICATION
mirror-dedupe stores every unique package file once in the pool, keyed
by its SHA-256 hash (pool/by-hash/SHA256/ab/cd/<hash>).  Pool entries
are hardlinked into each repo's pool/ tree.  When multiple repos or
architectures share identical files (same hash), they share the same
pool inode — no extra disk space is consumed.
.PP
A pool sweep (\-\-sweep-pool) walks the pool and removes files whose link
count has dropped to 1 (i.e., no repo references them anymore).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Sync all enabled mirrors:
.B mirror-dedupe \-\-sync
.TP
Sync specific mirror:
.B mirror-dedupe \-\-sync \-\-mirror ubuntu
.TP
Scan a repository and generate config:
.B mirror-dedupe \-\-scan \-\-name grafana \-\-out /etc/mirror-dedupe/repos-available https://apt.grafana.com
.TP
Test a mirror configuration:
.B mirror-dedupe \-\-test grafana
.TP
Activate a mirror:
.B mirror-dedupe \-\-activate grafana
.TP
Run pool orphan sweep:
.B mirror-dedupe \-\-sweep-pool
.TP
Create a snapshot of all repos:
.B mirror-dedupe \-\-snapshot
.TP
Restore latest snapshot for a repo:
.B mirror-dedupe \-\-restore-snapshot ubuntu
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/mirror-dedupe/
Default configuration directory.
.TP
.I /etc/mirror-dedupe/mirror-dedupe.conf
Main configuration file.
.TP
.I /etc/mirror-dedupe/repos-available/
Available mirror configurations.
.TP
.I /etc/mirror-dedupe/repos-enabled/
Enabled mirror configurations (symlinks to repos-available).
.TP
.I /srv/mirror/
Default mirror_root.
.TP
.I /srv/mirror/repos/
Repository tree (derived from mirror_root).
.TP
.I /srv/mirror/pool/
Content-addressable pool (derived from mirror_root).
.TP
.I /srv/mirror/mirror-dedupe/
Tool metadata directory (derived from mirror_root).
Contains one subdirectory per repo, each holding a \fBsync.lock\fR file
(an \fBflock\fR(2) exclusive lock held during sync) and a
\fBstats.ndjson\fR file (append-only sync history).
This directory is intentionally excluded from snapshots — lock files are
transient and stats are non-critical; restoring a snapshot leaves mirror
content correct regardless of whether stats are current.
This directory is safe to delete when no sync is running.
Deleting it during a sync removes the mutual exclusion that prevents
concurrent syncs on the same repo.
Use \fB\-\-stats-reset\fR to clear statistics via the normal CLI.
.SH SYSTEMD INTEGRATION
The package includes systemd timer and service units:
.TP
.B mirror-dedupe.timer
Scheduled timer that runs the sync daily at a randomised time between
00:00\(en06:00 UTC.
.TP
.B mirror-dedupe.service
Service unit that executes the sync.
.PP
To check timer status:
.RS
.B systemctl status mirror-dedupe.timer
.RE
.PP
To trigger a sync manually:
.RS
.B systemctl start mirror-dedupe.service
.RE
.PP
To view logs:
.RS
.B journalctl -u mirror-dedupe.service
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error occurred during synchronisation or deduplication.
